1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,549
Trained from scratch.

2
00:00:01,549 --> 00:00:02,513
In India.

3
00:00:02,513 --> 00:00:04,934
On those shared chips you just saw.

4
00:00:04,934 --> 00:00:10,011
And before it ever talked to you, it read around twelve trillion pieces of text.

5
00:00:10,011 --> 00:00:12,505
Then Sarvam did something generous.

6
00:00:12,505 --> 00:00:14,260
It made the model open.

7
00:00:14,260 --> 00:00:19,000
Any Indian developer can download it and build their own apps on it, for free.

8
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:23,560
The minister had hoped for six months, and later said ten at the most.

9
00:00:23,560 --> 00:00:25,031
It took about a year.

10
00:00:25,031 --> 00:00:27,863
Late, you could say... but delivered.

11
00:00:27,863 --> 00:00:32,057
And that same week, BharatGen — a team led by I.I.T.

12
00:00:32,057 --> 00:00:38,236
Bombay — showed its own model too, called Param Two, built for all twenty-two scheduled Indian languages.

13
00:00:38,236 --> 00:00:40,113
Now remember my promise to you.

14
00:00:40,113 --> 00:00:41,441
The chopping test.

15
00:00:41,441 --> 00:00:42,527
Same question.

16
00:00:42,527 --> 00:00:44,386
Will it rain in my village tomorrow?

17
00:00:44,386 --> 00:00:46,536
DeepSeek's chopper, you've seen.

18
00:00:46,536 --> 00:00:47,933
Hindi, eighteen.

19
00:00:47,933 --> 00:00:49,472
Marathi, twenty.

20
00:00:49,472 --> 00:00:51,056
Telugu, twenty-five.

21
00:00:51,056 --> 00:00:53,972
The chopper behind Chat G.P.T.'s recent models...

22
00:00:53,972 --> 00:00:57,632
Hindi eight, Marathi fourteen, Telugu fifteen.

23
00:00:57,632 --> 00:00:58,767
And Sarvam's?

24
00:00:58,767 --> 00:01:01,908
Hindi, eight — exactly the same as English.

25
00:01:01,908 --> 00:01:03,277
Marathi, ten.

26
00:01:03,277 --> 00:01:04,630
Telugu, eleven.

27
00:01:04,630 --> 00:01:06,844
And this isn't one lucky sentence.

28
00:01:06,844 --> 00:01:12,507
We ran the same test on more than a thousand sentences, each one in thirteen languages.

29
00:01:12,507 --> 00:01:13,614
Look at Odia.

30
00:01:13,614 --> 00:01:17,503
On DeepSeek's chopper, five and a half times the pieces of English.

31
00:01:17,503 --> 00:01:20,059
On Sarvam's... less than one and a half.

32
00:01:20,059 --> 00:01:22,635
And BharatGen's chopper does about as well.

33
00:01:22,635 --> 00:01:26,183
So for our language, the gap shrinks, a lot.

34
00:01:26,183 --> 00:01:29,840
Because this time... an Indian team put the missing pieces in.

